{
  "case_id": "2021-21-463",
  "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In enacting Senate Bill 8, the Texas legislature not only deliberately prohibited the exercise of a constitutional right recognized by this Court, it did everything it could to evade effective judicial protection of that right in federal or state court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, you rely on Ex parte Young to some extent, but Ex parte Young makes clear that federal courts cannot enjoin state judges. So how do you distinguish your case from the express language in Ex parte Young?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I read your complaint, and I thought you only asked for declaratory judgment against the judges and an injunction against the clerks. Did I misread your complaint?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We sought -- consistent with the text of Section 1983, we sought declaratory relief against judges and -- and an injunction against the clerks, and I --I think that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, counsel, the matters that you're talking about now, they're essential to your argument, right? You -- you agree that it would be adequate to have federal court review at the end of the state process but for the chilling effect that you're talking about, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: A judge may be enforcing a state law when the judge renders a decision based on that state law and provides relief based on that state law. But do you think a judge is enforcing a law when the judge merely begins to adjudicate the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HEARRON: We are requesting an injunction. So we have a --a pending class certification motion for a defendant class against the clerks, so we would be requesting an injunction against the commencement -- or the docketing of lawsuits against the clerks of the -- across the State of Texas, as well as injunctive relief against the state executive officials for their residual authority to enforce S.B. 8."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0001-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the real danger is, if this Court does not allow this suit, then that will provide a roadmap for other states to abrogate other rights that have been recognized by this Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners' pursuit of an injunction suffers from two fundamental problems. First, none of the individuals that Petitioners sued are appropriate defendants under well-established Article III and equitable principles. Second, Petitioners ask for an expansion of access to the federal courts that only Congress and not this Court may provide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Stone, the -- why wouldn't you consider the S.B. 8 plaintiffs to be sort of private attorneys general? If the attorney general or other state officials don't enforce the law, would it be that unusual to consider them as acting in concert with the state to enforce a state-preferred policy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are currently 14 pre-enforcement review challenges pending in a multi-district litigation in Travis County's state court. So, to speak to specifically your concern about federal court pre-enforcement access, no, that wouldn't change the Article III or sovereign immunity doctrines in play here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Okay, can I go back for a second from -- to -- from detail to the sort of general -- bigger picture, which stuck in my mind when I read all this road -- you know, roadmap. That should call up a lot of arguments in the briefs. And I thought of Holmes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Assume I disagree, because you didn't answer to my satisfaction"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Can I ask you about the implications of your position for other constitutional rights? The amicus brief of the Firearms Policy Coalition says, \"This will easily become the model for suppression of other constitutional rights, with Second Amendment rights being the most likely targets.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Firearms Policy Coalition",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0003-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\"This will easily become the model for suppression of other constitutional rights, with Second Amendment rights being the most likely targets.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Texas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State of Texas's position, Your Honor, is that the courts of the State of Texas will absolutely faithfully apply any decisions of this Court as they understand them to -- to apply to federal -- cases of federal law faithfully, and that the other officers inside -- the other officers within Texas are bound likewise to -- to take the interpretations from this Court and federal law and to faithfully implement them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 79,
        "start": 79
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "quick technical question. In reading Ex parte Young, I -- I got the impression that the enforcement mechanism was really private shippers or passengers who were supposed to sue the railroad. The attorney general didn't have any direct power. He just had a kind of residual power."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STONE: No more than that probably there's no such Ex parte Young remedy against individuals generally. Now, if multiple people acted in concert, they could all be joined."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: They're just on an individual-by-individual basis?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Marc A. Hearron",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HEARRON: I'd like to begin by picking up on the point that -- or the question that Justice Barrett was just asking. Those 14 pending state court proceedings, any relief would be against only those defendants who were sued in those proceedings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0004-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Texas has a declaratory judgment act that allows citizens to sue the --the State of Texas or a relative -- or the state agency under the Texas Declaratory Judgment Act to get that broader relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0004-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "S.B. 8 overrides the state declaratory judgment act and reasserts sovereign immunity to prevent exactly that kind of lawsuit against the state to seek broader review in state courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stone",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eced1b5b6fdff9d7d10d981c7a09b02fdde851a83dd48cfe364fc90e1aad17dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eced1b5b6fdf-0004-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Every single person would have to make the decision, am I willing to subject myself to the risk that I -- of $10,000 or more, it's a minimum liability per abortion, plus the risk that I'm going to be haled into suits all across"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-21-463",
